    {
      "id": "MJUe",
      "code_hash": "a3f1824f5eed215145beb6f9c87a7734",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><span class=\"paragraph\">Wave= several reports close to each other in space and time (DBSCAN on\nx, y, t, where one day is converted to KM_PER_DAY kilometres so that EPS means\n\"about X km or Y days\"). We then score each wave for a track-like pattern:\ndo the reports advance along one direction as time passes?</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Based on the sighting data, it is not possible to prove that the sightings involve the same UFO, but it is possible to identify waves of sightings (multiple reports occurring close to each other in both time and location) and determine whether the wave appears to follow a moving trajectory.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">!! So waves are candidates, not proof of the \"same\" object !! :D ^^</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
